# {{SERVER_NAME}}

An HTTPS MCP server scaffolded with the safe-MCP playbook. Read tools and write tools are physically separated; mutations are off by default behind a single visible env switch; queries are bounded; AI search is rate-limited; all telemetry goes to stderr; errors are typed and actionable.

## Quickstart

    bun install
    bun run gen:cert            # one-time: generate a localhost dev cert
    bun run dev                 # boot HTTPS server on port {{HTTPS_PORT}}
    bun run inspect             # boot stdio server + MCP inspector UI
    bun test                    # run unit + gate + stdout-discipline tests

## Environment variables

| Var                                     | Purpose                                                       | Default                  |
|-----------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------|
| `MCP_PORT`                              | HTTPS port                                                    | `{{HTTPS_PORT}}`         |
| `MCP_TLS_CERT` / `MCP_TLS_KEY`          | TLS material paths                                            | `./certs/dev-*.pem`      |
| `MCP_AUTH_MODE`                         | `oidc` / `api-key` / `both`                                   | `{{AUTH_MODE}}`          |
| `OIDC_ISSUER_URL` / `OIDC_AUDIENCE`     | OIDC validation                                               | unset (must set in prod) |
| `MCP_API_KEYS`                          | comma-separated keys, api-key mode only                       | unset                    |
| `BACKEND_BASE_URL`                      | upstream system of record                                     | `{{BACKEND_BASE_URL}}`   |
| `MCP_MUTATIONS_ENABLED`                 | **set to `true` to allow write tools**                        | `false`                  |
| `MCP_RATE_LIMIT_AI_SEARCH_PER_MIN`      | AI search per-user ceiling                                    | `6`                      |
| `MCP_MAX_RESULTS_CAP`                   | hard cap on search results                                    | `100`                    |

## Tool inventory

| Tool                  | Kind      | Notes                                                       |
|-----------------------|-----------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
| `search_companies`    | read      | Requires at least one filter; capped at 100 results.        |
| `get_company`         | read      | Returns `NOT_FOUND` typed error for unknown ids.            |
| `ai_search_companies` | read      | Rate-limited; configurable per-environment.                 |
| `create_ticket`       | write     | Off by default. Enable via `MCP_MUTATIONS_ENABLED=true`.    |

## The release-gate sequence

Before connecting any LLM client:

1. `bun test` — all unit tests green, including the mutation-gate negative test.
2. `bun run inspect` — open the MCP inspector, verify the tool count matches the table above.
3. Fire each read tool against the real backend. Confirm flat output shape.
4. With `MCP_MUTATIONS_ENABLED=false`: invoke `create_ticket`. Confirm `MUTATION_DISABLED` error mentions the env var.
5. With `MCP_MUTATIONS_ENABLED=true`: invoke `create_ticket` against a test backend. Confirm the success path.
6. Malformed input → `VALIDATION_FAILED` with a specific message.
7. AI search above the ceiling → `RATE_LIMITED` carrying the configured limit.

If any step fails, comment out the offending tool in `src/tools/registry.ts` with a `// FIXME(inspector):` note until fixed. Fail closed.

## Architecture

    src/
      server.ts          Streamable HTTP entry; mounts /mcp + /healthz
      config.ts          Env parsing into a typed Config
      auth.ts            OIDC / api-key verification, produces a Principal
      logger.ts          Structured stderr logger (never stdout)
      pipeline.ts        6-layer pipeline + mutation gate
      errors.ts          Typed error taxonomy
      ratelimit.ts       Per-user, per-tool token bucket
      backends/
        client.ts        BackendClient interface + typed records
        rest.ts          REST adapter
        graphql.ts       GraphQL adapter
        grpc.ts          gRPC adapter stub
      tools/
        registry.ts      Tool registry — read tools first, mutations last
        search-companies.ts        read
        get-company.ts             read
        ai-search-companies.ts     read (rate-limited)
        create-ticket.ts           write (gated)

## Adding new tools

Use the parent skill's `add-tool` mode. It enforces the same conventions automatically — no hand-rolling.
